  "methodology_notes": [
    "auto_adjust=True: on raw prices a stock split appears as a -50% daily return and would dominate any anomaly detection.",
    "All rolling windows are TRAILING. No centred windows, no full-sample statistics. Every value was computable on its date.",
    "Log returns, so multi-day returns aggregate additively.",
    "idio_vol removes sector movement via a rolling beta on KBE. This is the bank-specific risk measure and the one to use for anomaly detection.",
    "Rolling rather than fixed beta: bank betas rise during stress, and a fixed beta would use future data and mis-state residuals precisely when it matters most.",
    "peer_pctile is cross-sectional per date, so a sector-wide rise leaves rankings unchanged.",
    "Residual variance has no degrees-of-freedom correction for the estimated beta: a small constant downward bias in the level that does not affect relative anomaly detection.",
    "Yahoo revises historical data. 01_raw is the snapshot as downloaded at the run timestamp above; re-downloading may not reproduce it exactly."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Yahoo Finance is not an official exchange feed; minor discrepancies against vendor data are expected.",
    "Delistings and ticker changes are not handled \u2014 the peer group is assumed stable across the sample.",
    "No survivorship-bias correction: peers are chosen from banks that exist today.",
    "Corporate actions other than splits and dividends (spin-offs, mergers) are not adjusted for."
  ]
